  // THE BUILD PANEL'S FONT — `"FiraCode"` WAS A FAMILY NOBODY DECLARES.
  //
  // Reported as *"the font used in the build panel is not right"*, with no
  // further detail. Measured from the compiled theme (byte-identical to the
  // one noirstudio.dev serves): the whole design system declares exactly four
  // `@font-face` families — `SpaceGrotesk`, `SpaceMono`, `FiraMono` and
  // `FontAwesome`. **`FiraCode` is not one of them, and no FiraCode file
  // exists in the tree.** It is dead text in 21 places, four of them here.
  //
  // Elsewhere that mistake is survivable because the rule writes a fallback —
  // `components/shell.styl` and `components/problems.styl` say
  // `"FiraCode", monospace`, so the pane degrades to the platform's monospace
  // and merely looks off-brand. These four rules had NO second entry. An
  // unresolvable family with no generic fallback drops to the browser's
  // *default standard font*, which on Chrome is a PROPORTIONAL SERIF — so
  // column-aligned compiler output was being set in Times beside a terminal
  // set in SpaceMono. That is the visible difference the report is pointing
  // at, and the `!important` meant nothing downstream could rescue it.
  //
  // `SpaceMono` rather than `FiraMono` — which is declared, and is probably
  // what the typo was reaching for. The neighbours decide it: TERMINAL OUTPUT
  // is SpaceMono (`components/terminal.styl`), the EVENT LOG is SpaceMono,
  // and the editor is `CODE_FONT_FAMILY = "SpaceMono, monospace"`
  // (`frontend/utils.nim`). Build output is read against those, not against a
  // font the product uses nowhere.
  //
  // The generic fallback is written even though `SpaceMono` IS declared,
  // because that is the property whose absence turned a typo into a serif.
  .build-output-container
    flex: 1
    overflow: auto
    font-family: "SpaceMono", monospace !important
    font-size: 14px
    line-height: 24px
    white-space: pre-wrap

    .build-stdout, .build-stderr, .build-output-line
      min-height: 24px
      padding-left: 0.5em
      font-family: "SpaceMono", monospace !important
      font-size: 14px
      line-height: 24px
      white-space: pre-wrap

