#active-notifications
  width: fit-content
  height: fit-content
  bottom: NOTIFICATION_STACK_BOTTOM
  display: flex
  // `column-reverse`, so the newest toast is at the BOTTOM of the stack and
  // the lowest one on screen is the FIRST DOM child. The clipped notification
  // in the report was therefore `:first-child`, not `:last-child`.
  flex-direction: column-reverse
  gap: NOTIFICATION_STACK_GAP
  position: fixed
  z-index: 100
  // HORIZONTALLY CENTRED, and this replaces `right: 8px`.
  //
  // THE DEFECT IT FIXES, measured on the live deployment (revision b6e28026):
  // the durability notice — 466px wide, `bottom: 3rem`, anchored to the right
  // edge — sat over the lower ~180px of the CONSTRAINTS column, which is the
  // pane a visitor opens to read their circuit's generated code. It is the one
  // notice in the product that is raised on a first visit and stays until it
  // is dismissed, so the overlap was not a flash: it was the default first
  // screen, in every screenshot taken of it.
  //
  // NOT CAUSED BY THE PREVIOUS FIX IN THIS FILE, which is worth stating
  // because the two look related. 44abd587a moved this stack from
  // `bottom: 38px` to `NOTIFICATION_STACK_BOTTOM` and changed nothing on this
  // axis; `right: 8px` has been the anchor since the toasts were first placed
  // (adc508550, March 2025), and the notice only started landing on a pane
  // when 3850bd9b8 moved it out of its own body-level banner and into this
  // stack. That commit fixed a notice that covered the STATUS BAR by putting
  // it where it covers a PANE instead.
  //
  // WHY CENTRE RATHER THAN THE OTHER CORNER. In this product's three-column
  // edit layout the bottom corners belong to the two NARROW columns — FILES at
  // 20% and CONSTRAINTS at 25% — and both of those are lists whose content
  // runs the full height of the pane, so a toast in either corner covers rows
  // somebody is reading. The centre belongs to the editor, which is 55% wide
  // and whose text is anchored to the TOP: the region a 466px toast occupies
  // there is empty in the common case and is one keystroke from being scrolled
  // clear in the rest. Moving it to `left: 8px` would also collide with
  // `.debug-notification`, which is already anchored there.
  //
  // `left: 50%` + `translateX(-50%)` rather than `margin: auto`, because the
  // element is `position: fixed` with `width: fit-content` and no `right`, so
  // there is no resolved free space for `auto` margins to divide.
  left: 50%
  transform: translateX(-50%)


#status
  position: relative
  width: 100vw
  display: flex
  flex-direction: column-reverse
  font-family: "SpaceGrotesk"

  // Toasts stack above the bar and carry buttons; they must never become a
  // window handle if one ever overlaps the footer.
  > #active-notifications
    -webkit-app-region: no-drag


  #status-base
    // Hosts the auto-hide bottom tab strip (#auto-hide-bottom-strip) alongside
    // the status bar's own content, per
    // `codetracer-specs/Planned-Features/Auto-Hide-Panes.md` §3.1:
    //
    //   |-- Status Bar / Footer
    //   |     |-- Left: auto-hide tab labels for bottom-pinned panels
    //   |     |-- Right: existing status bar content (language, encoding, location)
    //
    // ... and §10.3, which places the collapsed-strip icon zone
    // (`#auto-hide-collapsed-icon-zone`) in the same bar.
    //
    // DO NOT hide `#status-base`'s children as a group, IN ANY SPELLING —
    // including ones that leave the box intact and only move it out of view.
    // A `> *:not(#auto-hide-bottom-strip) { display: none !important }` rule has
    // been written here twice — b27da3947 "feat: Redesign of the status bar"
    // and, after it was removed, 51a3e820e "fix: UI regressions" — and both
    // times it made the bar tabs-only.  A third attempt, 00fd68b7f "fix: status
    // bar styling", reached the same result with `position: absolute;
    // left: -9999px` on `#file-info-status` and `.status-right`, and shipped
    // undetected for two weeks because that is precisely the family the guards
    // below document themselves as unable to see (they ask whether a region has
    // a box, and an off-screen region has one).  The wish behind all three is
    // reasonable: a quieter footer.  No such form can deliver it, because
    // every child of this bar is either required by the design or invisible
    // in production
    // already (enumerated on a live launch: `#auto-hide-collapsed-icon-zone`,
    // `#file-info-status`, `#auto-hide-bottom-strip`, `.test-movement` — which
    // renders only under `data.startOptions.inTest` — and `.status-right`).
    // There is no "legacy" residue left to hide; hiding the group means hiding
    // the design.  A quieter footer has to come from restyling or from removing
    // a specific readout in the design doc first.
    //
    // Concretely, the rule silently deletes three surfaces that no other part
    // of the UI provides:
    //
    //   * `.location-path` + `#copy-path-image` — the only place the current
    //     debug location (`path:line#ticks`) is displayed at all; nothing else
    //     in the frontend renders `StatusBaseModel.locationText`, and the only
    //     other copy-a-path affordance is the editor tab's "Copy full path"
    //     context-menu entry (`ui/layout.nim`), which copies the tab label,
    //     not the location the debugger is actually stopped at.
    //   * `#file-info-status` — language / encoding / `stable: ready`.
    //   * `#auto-hide-collapsed-icon-zone` — the `!important` beat
    //     `.collapsed-icon-zone.has-icons`, so the Auto-Hide-Panes §10.3 icon
    //     zone could never appear even when panels were collapsed.
    //
    // The layout the spec asks for falls out of the DOM order in
    // `viewmodel/views/isonim_status_view.nim` once nothing is force-hidden:
    // icon zone and `#file-info-status` on the left, the tab strip taking the
    // slack (`#auto-hide-bottom-strip { flex: 1 }`), `.status-right` (location
    // + copy button) pinned to the right edge.
    //
    // The constraint is checked against the BUILT stylesheet, on effect rather
    // than on wording, by
    // `src/tests/gui/tests/status-bar/footer-visibility-css-guard.spec.ts`:
    // it lays out this bar in a browser with the compiled theme CSS applied and
    // fails if any required region computes to no box.  Any spelling that
    // removes the box trips it, however the selector is written — `:not()`,
    // `:where()`, `:has()`, an enumerated list, `@media`, `display`,
    // `visibility`, `opacity`, `transform: scale(0)`, or the same applied to an
    // ancestor.  `status-bar-footer-contract.spec.ts` pins the same contract
    // against the real Electron app.
    //
    // What it does NOT catch, so you know what you are not covered against:
    // rules that keep the box and only change the painting — moving the bar
    // off-screen, `clip-path`, `filter: opacity(0)`, or drawing text in the
    // background colour.  Those pass both guards.  Run the app and look at the
    // footer before shipping anything in that family.
    //
    // NOTE the guard reads the COMPILED theme, so it only sees an edit to this
    // file after `just build-once`.
    bottom: 0
    background-color: colors-ui-surface-primary-default
    // THE BAR'S HEIGHT IS READ FROM A VALUE, and `#active-notifications`
    // reads the same one. These used to be `2em`/`0.25em` here and a bare
    // `38px` there, which is how the toast stack came to address a bar edge
    // that had moved. See the header of this file.
    height: STATUS_BAR_CONTENT_HEIGHT
    font-size: 1rem    // reset from 0.75rem so the rem values above land 1:1
    position: fixed
    width: 100%
    z-index: 100 !important
    display: flex
    align-items: stretch
    overflow: visible   // allow tab curve pseudo-elements to bleed above the bar
    padding-top: STATUS_BAR_VERTICAL_PADDING    // curves visible above the tabs
    padding-bottom: STATUS_BAR_VERTICAL_PADDING // mirrors side-strip padding

    // The footer drags the window, like the caption bar does.
    //
    // Same arrangement as `#menu` (components/menu_bar.styl) and
    // `.session-tab-bar` (components/session_tabs.styl): the bar drags, and the
    // things it holds opt out, so only the space between them is a handle.
    // Declared on the bar rather than on the empty area because there is no
    // element for the empty area — it is whatever the tab strip does not fill.
    -webkit-app-region: drag

    // Readouts and controls behave normally: `.status-right` carries the
    // location text, and text inside a drag region cannot be selected.
    > *
      -webkit-app-region: no-drag

    // ...except the tab strip, which is `flex: 1` and so spans the whole bar
    // (components/auto_hide.styl).  Marking it `no-drag` with the rest would
    // freeze the footer end to end, because the empty area IS the strip's
    // unfilled remainder — the same mistake the caption bar's left region made,
    // where a `no-drag` container froze the 300-odd px of bar beside the debug
    // toolbar.  So the strip drags and its tabs opt out individually.
    > #auto-hide-bottom-strip
      -webkit-app-region: drag

      .auto-hide-strip-tab
        -webkit-app-region: no-drag

